{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Tempered, pure.</b> It appears that the meaning of ״pure״ is that no admixture of colors should be visible in it, for since it contains eleven spices, the colors will multiply; and even though one mixes them together, because of the multiplicity of spices and the large quantity — three hundred and sixty-eight maneh — some corner of it will remain where the color is not uniform. And even if it should be uniform, nevertheless when one examines with the subtlety of visual perception he will discern that it is not a single color, and such a substance is not called ״pure.״ Therefore it says <b>tempered, pure</b> — meaning clear, so that a single color appears literally, through the thoroughness of the masterful blend, and through its being ground exceedingly fine."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:39.584686265Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}